From bae47cb2729d1cced219b1684009ec86d472bc1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 02:26:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix the findings of the review of the update on the device
 and of AssembledOperator

- update and revert of a behaviour integrated on the device end with the
  synchronization of the state arrays on the host (copies on the device
  invalidated), as on the host: a direct write in the state after an
  update is taken into account; the tangent operator blocks are set to
  zero on the host instead of being copied;
- Newton correction: a failure of the assembly of the tangent operator or
  of the setup of the linear solver on a process is made collective
  before the resolution; during the resolution, only the failures reported
  on all the processes (CollectiveFailure, thrown by
  raiseOnFailureOnAnyProcess) are caught in parallel;
- AssembledOperator: the number of assemblies of the assembled tangent
  operator, shared by the problem and its providers, tells the
  preconditioner whether the operator on which it is set up is still
  valid: it is set up again otherwise (the operator was assembled again by
  another call); an operator which is not a provider, such as the matrix
  of the prediction, keeps a valid setup instead of resetting the period;
- BatchIntegrationTest: direct write in the state after an update; the
  diagonal of the matrix-free operator is also checked with the assembled
  preconditioner, and a case without prediction keeps the preconditioner
  between time steps;
- comments updated.
